cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these corpora, please cite them as below."
type: dataset
title: "Agent Movement: research notes and curated news and paper corpora on portable, interoperable AI-agent work"
authors:
  - family-names: "Seyedkazemi Ardebili"
    given-names: "Mohsen"
    website: "https://mskazemi.github.io"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MSKazemi/agent-movement"
url: "https://github.com/MSKazemi/agent-movement"
# The first paragraph of the abstract is the positioning statement; tests/test_positioning.py
# requires it to match README.md and both agenda docs byte for byte.
abstract: >-
  Agent Movement is a research prototype: an open, evidence-first testbed built to make claims about safely moving AI-agent work between executors falsifiable. It currently pairs ranked research questions with synthetic, localhost-only Python prototypes and MobilityBench v0.1, a frozen, deterministic, LLM-free benchmark of 18 synthetic tasks that scores keeping, restarting, delegating (locally or over A2A) and checkpoint-relocating work under injected faults, with the A2A and relocation modes enabled by optional extras, and reports refusals and unavailable baselines instead of hiding them. It is not production software, a new agent protocol or a rival to A2A or MCP.

  The repository studies how AI-agent work
  can move between agents, frameworks, models, machines and organizations
  without losing relevant context, accountability or safety controls. It
  distinguishes delegation, portable task context, runtime relocation and
  cross-framework migration, and contains research notes on protocols,
  security, forensics and device compatibility. It also contains two curated,
  independently audited corpora: 100 dated news items (2024-2026) and 83
  metadata-verified scholarly papers (1980-2026), each with structured records,
  summaries and BibTeX.
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - agent movement
  - agent interoperability
  - agent migration
  - mobile agents
  - delegation
  - Model Context Protocol
  - MCP
  - Agent2Agent
  - A2A
  - durable execution
  - agent security
  - research corpus
  - literature corpus
